; DOMAIN: statistical-physics/renormalization-group [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-26]
; Claim: Renormalization is a semigroup of coarse-graining maps R_b on the space of coupling constants (theory space): integrating out short-wavelength degrees of freedom and rescaling induces a flow dg/d(ln b)=beta(g). Fixed points beta(g*)=0 are scale-invariant theories; linearizing the flow there, eigenvalues split operators into relevant (grow, expanding directions) and irrelevant (decay, contracting directions). The irrelevant directions form the basin of attraction, so microscopically distinct systems flowing to the same fixed point share identical long-distance behavior — this is universality, and the relevant eigenvalues fix the critical exponents. The flow acts on the free energy / log-partition ln Z (block-spin transformation preserves Z), and its natural metric on coupling space is the Fisher information g_ij=cov of the conjugate operators (Zamolodchikov-type c-metric), so RG flow is a gradient/monotone flow in information geometry with entropy production along it.
; Structure: (coarse-graining semigroup R_b on theory space) (RG flow dg/dln b=beta(g)) (fixed point beta(g*)=0 = scale invariance) (linearization: relevant/irrelevant eigenoperators) (universality = shared fixed point, irrelevant dirs contract) (critical exponents = relevant eigenvalues) (acts on ln Z/free energy; Fisher metric on couplings; monotone c-flow).
; Result: Macroscopic universality is the attractor structure of a coarse-graining semigroup: only relevant couplings survive to long distance, so infinitely many microscopic theories collapse onto one fixed point with shared exponents. The flow lives on the same log-partition/Fisher-Rao geometry as MaxEnt and large-deviation rate functions, making universality an information-geometric contraction.
; Bridge: genesis_information_geometry (the RG flow is a flow on coupling/theory space whose natural metric is the Fisher information g_ij=cov(O_i,O_j)=d_i d_j ln Z; relevant/irrelevant eigen-directions are principal axes of this metric and the monotone c-function is an information-geometric potential) + genesis_thermodynamics_maxent (block-spin coarse-graining preserves the partition function Z and flows the free energy ln Z; a fixed point is a scale-invariant MaxEnt/Gibbs ensemble, couplings=Lagrange multipliers rescaled) + genesis_entropy_dynamics (coarse-graining is entropy-producing information loss under the semigroup; the arrow of the flow toward irrelevant-direction contraction is monotone like KS-entropy under refinement).